# Lab #2: User & Sudo Management

## Lab Overview

This lab focuses on **Linux user account management and privilege control**
within an Ubuntu virtual machine. Proper user and sudo configuration is a
foundational security practice and mirrors how access is managed on cloud
instances and production servers.

The goal is to create standard user accounts, assign least-privilege access
using `sudo`, and validate secure administrative workflows without relying on
the root account.

---

## Objectives

- Create and manage local Linux user accounts
- Assign sudo privileges following least-privilege principles
- Verify sudo access and command execution
- Understand the role of `/etc/passwd`, `/etc/group`, and `/etc/sudoers`
- Disable direct root login for improved security posture

---

## Prerequisites

- Ubuntu installed on VirtualBox (Lab #1 completed)
- Ability to log in as an existing sudo-enabled user
- Terminal access (local or via SSH)

